# What NOT to upload to the EAS build workers.
#
# EAS falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent — which was the problem: dist/ and
# temp-export-*/ are LISTED in .gitignore but were committed before it, and ignore rules do
# not apply to already-tracked files. So ~14.7 MB of dead build output was uploaded on every
# single build.
#
# This costs zero APK bytes — metro.config.js already blocks both paths from the Metro crawl,
# and nothing in them is reachable from AppEntry. The win is upload and queue time, not size.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file REPLACES .gitignore for uploads rather than adding to it, so anything
# that must stay off the build workers has to be repeated here. .env especially: it is
# gitignored today, and dropping it would start shipping local values — including the
# localhost EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL — into cloud builds. Production values come from the EAS
# environment, not from this directory.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

node_modules

# Committed build output. Untracked with `git rm -r --cached dist temp-export-*`, but listed
# here too so a stray re-export never reaches the workers.
dist/
temp-export-*/
.expo/

# Local-only tooling and scratch.
coverage/
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
.agents/
.codex/
.mimocode/

# Generated by prebuild on the worker; a local copy would be stale and would override it.
android/
ios/

# Documentation. Deliberately NOT excluding assets/ or public/: assets/store/ holds only a
# 432 KB listing graphic and public/ is 40 KB, so the saving is noise — but app.json's
# web.favicon points into assets/store/, and a config that resolves locally while failing on
# a worker is a far worse trade than a few hundred kilobytes.
*.md
!README.md
